  "data": {
    "id": 825306,
    "name": "Chanterelle mushrooms",
    "description": "<p>Pacific Golden Chanterelles&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Cantharellus formosus</p><br />\n<p>Foraged weekly in the Coastal Range, these bright orange funnel-shaped mushrooms have a mild, sweet smell. They have a mild sweetness and umami flavor as well as a subtle earthy, nutty undertone. Excellent in pasta, on toast, and can be used in most recipes requiring cooked mushrooms.</p><br />\n<p>Basic preparation: heat pan over medium heat, quarter the mushrooms lengthwise, put mushrooms in heated pan, allow moisture to release, add a pinch of salt and fat of your choice once most water has evaporated, continue to cook for another 5-8 minutes, can be added to other dishes.</p>",
